7: /// walks a directory tree under the user profile breadth first without following directory links or other
8: /// reparse points, and skips the contents of any directory whose listing fails with an IO or access error
9: /// (an untrusted mount point, an access-denied or vanished folder), so a scan never fails on what it cannot
10: /// traverse.
11: /// </summary>
12: /// <remarks>
13: /// A directory is yielded when its parent lists it, unless it is a link; its contents are walked only when its own
14: /// listing succeeds. File links are yielded as files. Listing errors other than <see cref="IOException"/> and
15: /// <see cref="UnauthorizedAccessException"/> propagate. A scan root below the user profile or home is walked only
16: /// when <see cref="IsReachable"/> holds for it (hostile validation round 5 finding R5-F1; operator 2026-10-21:
17: /// "Fix both, strengthen ACs").
18: /// </remarks>
