56:     /// <summary>
57:     /// FR-MCP-018 ac-1, AC-FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGCTX-001-008: whether <paramref name="root"/> may be walked from
58:     /// <paramref name="boundary"/>: the root and every folder between the boundary and it must each be listed by
59:     /// its parent as a directory that is not a link or other reparse point. The boundary itself is trusted (a user
60:     /// profile or home that is itself a link is still scanned) and its parent is never listed; a root that is the
61:     /// boundary is reachable without any listing.
62:     /// </summary>
63:     /// <remarks>
64:     /// A folder whose listing fails with an <see cref="IOException"/> or <see cref="UnauthorizedAccessException"/>
65:     /// cannot be traversed, so the root is not reachable; any other listing error propagates. A root that is not
66:     /// below the boundary, or that a parent does not list as a directory, is not reachable.
67:     /// </remarks>
68:     /// <param name="boundary">The trusted folder the scan starts from (the user profile or home).</param>
69:     /// <param name="root">The scan root below <paramref name="boundary"/>.</param>
